course: dictionary
lesson: 5693
title: A word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Locust» is a good example. Its main meaning is a large grasshopper, but the words around it show which meaning is in use.
explain: «Desert locusts are grasshoppers that, when crowded, change colour and behaviour and form swarms of billions that eat crops.» The words grasshoppers, swarms and crops tell you this is the insect, not a tree or a story.
explain: «In the Bible John the Baptist ate locusts and wild honey.» Here the Bible is the clue. Locusts are an insect in this story, and they are also one of the plagues of Egypt in the Book of Exodus. A dictionary lists these meanings separately, so check the context before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A locust is a large kind of grasshopper that sometimes gathers in huge swarms.
fact: «A swarm of locusts» means a large group of locusts flying together.
fact: In the Bible, locusts are one of the plagues of Egypt in the Book of Exodus.
fact: Some people in the US call a cicada, a loud buzzing insect, a locust, and a locust tree is a different thing again.
exercise: «A big locust swarm can eat as much food in a day as millions of people.» What is a locust? | A small bird that sings at dawn | A kind of fish that lives in rivers | *A large kind of grasshopper | A shady tree in a park
exercise: «Insects can also be fierce: a swarm of locusts can strip whole farms.» Find and copy the word that means a large group flying together. | farms | fierce | *swarm | insects
exercise: Some people in the US call a loud buzzing insect a locust. Which insect is this? | A butterfly | A ladybird | A bee | *A cicada
test: «In the Bible John the Baptist ate locusts and wild honey.» In this sentence, what are locusts? | *An insect that people ate | A kind of honey | A plague of rain | A tall tree
test: «About two billion people around the world eat insects, and more than 1,900 kinds are eaten: grasshoppers in Mexico, big caterpillars in southern Africa, queen ants in Colombia, locusts in parts of the Middle East and Africa.» Which word in this sentence tells you locusts are food here? | Mexico | billion | *eat | kinds
exam: «Locusts are still eaten in parts of the Middle East and Africa.» Which meaning of locust fits this sentence best? | A plague of rain from the sky | A kind of tree that grows in dry places | *A large kind of grasshopper | A loud buzzing insect in the US
